.SH "GLOBAL"
.SH "NAME"
.PP
\fIglobal\fP \- hold global server properties

.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
\fIglobal\fP holds global server properties, like the prometheus metrics port and root directory.
It only implements the \fB\fCSetupper\fR interface and it's not a handler and you can not use it as such.

.SH "SYNTAX"
.PP
.RS

.nf
root DIRECTORY
metrics [/N] [ADDRRES]
debug

.fi
.RE

.IP \(bu 4
with \fIroot\fP \fBDIRECTORY\fP is the directory to use as the root directory for the server. Any relative path names will
get this directory prefixed. If \fBDIRECTORY\fP itself is also relative the current working directory (cwd) of the testserv
process will be prefixed.
.IP \(bu 4
with \fIdebug\fP the global log level is to debug.
.IP \(bu 4
The \fImetrics\fP property allows setting the listening \fBADDRESS\fP for the promtheus metrics. This defaults to \fB\fClocalhost:9153\fR.
Without \fImetrics\fP no metrics can be scraped as the prometheus server isn't running, i.e. to allow for
metrics gathering \fImetrics\fP must be enabled in the global section.
The optional \fB/N\fP tells the metric handler to monitor 1 in \fBN\fP queries. The default is 10. This needs to
be a positive integer > 0.


.SH "EXAMPLES"
.PP
.RS

.nf
{
    root /var/lib/testserv
    metrics localhost:9152
}

.fi
.RE
